  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Security fix: sensitive HTTP headers are now redacted in diagnostic output.\n\n      Previously AuthenticatedHttpClientHandler joined every request and response header, key and\n      value, into its Debug level log message. The handler assigns the Authorization header a bearer\n      token nine lines earlier, so a usable access token was written verbatim. Any consumer running at\n      Debug retained usable credentials for the life of its log store.\n\n      Authorization, Proxy-Authorization, Cookie, Set-Cookie and common API key headers are now\n      redacted, case-insensitively, on request and response, along with any vendor-prefixed variant\n      whose name ends in \"Authorization\". The scheme and credential length are retained, so requests\n      remain diagnosable. The log line format is otherwise unchanged.\n\n      Consumers should upgrade and then review existing Debug logs for previously captured tokens.\n\n      Also in this release: removed internal error-level logging of token-refresh\n      (GenerateAccessTokenAsync) failures - callers already catch and log this with context, so it was\n      being logged twice.",
